      "side": 1,
      "message": "Austin: Given the information from Skia folks that it is a long-term goal for them to generalize their BGL (which would of course necessitate the fully general transform on the Dawn/Tint side), I don\u0027t think that it\u0027s worth the churn to introduce the concept of a \"combined sampler/texture\" entry at the Dawn API level - especially given that the Dawn-level transform is straightforward (I will of course validate that YCbCr sampler entries are followed by texture entries in the BGL). \nHowever, let me know if you think differently. I figure that we can in any case move forward with this implementation to unblock things even if we decide to then follow up immediately by adding that API-level construct and using it in Skia.",
      "revId": "fba45ffc8efb366cdb232ca5f3b996aeb84f3ce3",
